          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+type+theory"} dependent type theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identity+type"} identity type
            where elements from two different types can be compared for equality. Given types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            and an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+types"} equivalence of types
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:A \simeq B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x:A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y:B
            is a type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Id}_{A,B}(e, x, y)
            whose elements witness that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
            are “equal” over or modulo the equivalence
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
          %p
            The phrase “two-type identity type” is a placeholder name for a concept which may or may not have another name in the type theory literature. The idea however is that two-type identity types are the “non-dependent” versions of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dependent+identity+types"} dependent identity types
            in that it directly compares elements between two equivalent types, rather than between a family of dependent types which are equivalent via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transport"} transport
            across an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/identification"} identification
            in the index type.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Given types
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inductive+family"} inductive family
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/types"} types
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ≃
                  %mi B
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo :
                  %mi B
                  %mo ⊢
                  %msub
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Id
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi B
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e:A \simeq B, x:A, y:B \vdash \mathrm{Id}_{A, B}(e, x, y)
          %p generated by the family of elements
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo :
                  %mi A
